    "linkedin:1168fd58612fbbdc0ca714c8": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Frontend Engineer II, Portfolio - Remote Opportunity",
        "company": "Torentify",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482044561",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": false,
        "description": "**About the Company** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Coinbase is a remote\\-first financial technology company focused on increasing economic freedom. The company builds products that help people manage and understand their digital assets. While employees work remotely, teams come together quarterly for in\\-person working sessions known as “surges.”\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**About the Role** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Coinbase is seeking a Senior Frontend Engineer to join its Portfolio team within the Consumer \\& Business group. The team develops the balances, holdings, and profit\\-and\\-loss (PnL) experiences used by millions of customers across the Coinbase app and website. In this role, you will turn complex, real\\-time financial data into clear, reliable, and accessible interfaces for users ranging from first\\-time buyers to experienced traders.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n You will work across web technologies, including React and TypeScript, and collaborate on native mobile experiences for iOS and Android. The role involves owning complex features from initial planning through production, improving frontend architecture, and helping maintain high engineering standards.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Key Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Own the design and delivery of core Portfolio experiences, including balances, holdings, and profit\\-and\\-loss features across web and native mobile platforms.\n* Build performant, accessible, and pixel\\-accurate user interfaces that display real\\-time financial data at Coinbase scale.\n* Collaborate with backend engineers, designers, and product partners to define requirements and take ambiguous problems from initial scoping through production rollout.\n* Drive frontend architecture and code quality, including component reuse, state management, testing, and performance instrumentation.\n* Conduct thorough code reviews and provide technical mentorship to strengthen engineering practices across the team.\n* Document architecture decisions and contribute to maintaining high standards for frontend development.\n* Integrate frontend experiences with backend APIs and ensure that data\\-intensive interfaces remain responsive and reliable.\n* Use generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight while improving workflow efficiency, cost, and quality through measurable outcomes.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Required Qualifications** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* 5\\+ years of frontend engineering experience building consumer\\-facing web applications with high\\-quality, well\\-tested production code.\n* Deep expertise in React and TypeScript, with a strong understanding of modern frontend fundamentals, including state management, rendering performance, and accessibility.\n* Demonstrated experience delivering and owning complex features end\\-to\\-end in production.\n* Experience building real\\-time or high\\-throughput user interfaces and integrating them with REST or GraphQL APIs.\n* Ability to work closely with design and product partners to shape product outcomes.\n* Experience using generative AI responsibly, with appropriate human oversight to ensure business\\-ready results and measurable improvements in efficiency, cost, or quality.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Preferred Qualifications** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Experience developing financial, trading, or other data\\-intensive applications where accuracy and latency are important.\n* Experience contributing to frontend architecture, technical documentation, code quality, and engineering mentorship.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Work Environment** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Coinbase operates as a remote\\-first, but not remote\\-only, company. Employees are expected to participate in quarterly in\\-person team working sessions known as “surges.”\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Salary and Benefits** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The annual base salary range for this position is $186,065–$218,900 USD, excluding equity and bonuses. Base salary varies by location. Total compensation may also include equity, bonus eligibility, and medical, dental, vision, and 401(k) benefits.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Application Limit** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Candidates may submit a maximum of three applications within a six\\-month period.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Equal Employment Opportunity** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Coinbase is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. Applicants with criminal histories will be considered in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Accommodations and Applicant Notices** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Applicants who need a reasonable accommodation due to a disability may email their request and contact information to accommodations\\[at]coinbase.com. US applicants may review the Employee Rights, Know Your Rights, and E\\-Verify Notice of Participation information. By submitting an application, candidates agree to the Candidate Privacy Notice; US applicants also agree to the Arbitration of Disputes.",
